OFFICE of the Board of Street and Water Commissioners Of the City OF Newark.


Newark, N. J., June 3, 1910.
Sealed proposals will be received at this office from 8 a. m. to 3 p. m. and opened by the board to be held at said time and place, for the paving and repairing of the following streets:


MT. PROSPECT AVENUE,
from Mt. Prospect avenue to Lake street;


BLEECKER STREET,
from High street to Lock street;


COMMERCIAL STREET,
from Railroad place easterly about 50 feet;
from East Kinney street northerly about 1888 feet;


HACKETT STREET,
from Plane street westerly about 26 feet;


MAY STREET,
from Lincoln avenue to Summer avenue;


PERSONS ALLEY,
from Market street to Bank street;


PLUM STREET,
from Washington street to Plane street;


RIDGE STREET,
from Park avenue to Second avenue.


The following is about the amount OF the work to be done, and the materials to be furnished for said work, and upon which bids will be taken:


FOR MT. PROSPECT AVENUE PAVING:
Five thousand nine hundred and seventy (5,970) square yards of brick pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
Four hundred and sixty-five (465) lineal feet of new 20 by 5 inch four cut curb set in concrete;
Two thousand (2,000) lineal feet of old curb set in concrete;

One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Standard prices will be paid for the following:
Eight (8) sets new 20 by 5 inch four cut corners set in concrete;
Five (5) new noiseless manhole covers;
One hundred and ninety (190) lineal feet of new 10 by 8 inch header curb set in concrete.


FOR BLEECKER STREET PAVING:
Thirty-seven hundred (3,700) square yards OF brick pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
Eighteen hundred (1,800) lineal feet of new 20 by 4 inch four cut curb set IN concrete;
Two hundred and fifty (250) lineal feet OF old curb four cut and reset in concrete;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Four (4) sets new 20 by 5 inch four cut corners;
Six (6) noiseless manhole covers;
Sixty-two (62) lineal feet OF new header curb.


FOR COMMERCIAL STREET PAVING:
Twelve hundred (1,200) square yards OF granite block pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
Eight hundred and forty (840) lineal feet new 16 by 8 inch four cut curb set in concrete;
Two hundred and eight (208) square feet new Belgian bridging laid on concrete;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Standard prices will be paid for the following:
Three (3) sets new 16 by 8 inch corners set in concrete.


FOR EAST KINNEY PLACE REPAVING:
Seven hundred (700) square yards of brick pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Standard prices will be paid for the following:
Four hundred (400) lineal feet new header curb set in concrete;
Three (3) new noiseless manhole covers.


FOR HACKETT STREET PAVING:
Six hundred and sixty (660) square yards OF brick pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
Five hundred (500) lineal feet of new 10 by 6 inch four cut curb set in concrete;
One hundred and ninety-two (192) square feet of new Belgian bridging laid on concrete;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Standard prices will be paid for the following:
One (1) set new 10 by 5 inch four cut corners set in concrete.


FOR MAY STREET PAVING:
One thousand eight hundred and twenty (1,820) square yards OF brick paving on a six inch concrete foundation;
Two hundred and fifty-five (255) lineal feet of new 20 by 4 inch four cut curb set in concrete;
Nine hundred (900) lineal feet OF old curb four cut and reset in concrete;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill ON old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Standard prices will be paid for the following:
Two (2) sets new 20 by 4 inch four cut corners;
Three (3) new noiseless manhole covers;
Sixty-two (62) lineal feet OF new header curb.


FOR PERSONS ALLEY REPAVING:
Five hundred (500) square yards OF new brick pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
Five (5) lineal feet of new 16 by 8 inch four cut curb set in concrete;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Standard prices will be paid for the following:
One (1) set new 10 by 8 inch four cut corners set in concrete;
Six (6) hundred (600) lineal feet of new header curb.


FOR PLUM STREET REPAVING:
Nine hundred and forty (940) square yards OF brick pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
One hundred (100) new 16 by 8 inch four cut curb set in concrete;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Two (2) sets new 16 by 8 inch four cut corners set in concrete;
Forty-two (42) lineal feet OF header curb &c. in concrete.


FOR RIDGE STREET PAVING:
Eight thousand four hundred and fifty (8,450) square yards OF brick pavement on a six inch concrete foundation;
Fifteen hundred (1,500) lineal feet OF new 20 by 4 inch four cut curb set in concrete;
Three thousand five hundred and fifty (3,550) lineal feet of old curb four cut and reset in concrete;
One (1) new basin complete;
One (1) new basin using old head and sill;
One (1) new head and sill on old basin;
One (1) new manhole complete with noiseless cover.

Standard prices will be paid for the following:

(Author Unknown.)
Would'st thou be wretched? It's an
easy way:
Think but of self, and self alone, all
day;
Think of thy pain, thy grief, thy loss,
thy care;
Think of thy good, thy pleasure, Oh
thy gain;
Think only of thyself; it will not be
vain.
Would'st thou be happy? Take an
easy way;
Think of those round thee—live for
them all day;
Think of their pain, their loss, their
grief, their care;
All that they have to do, or feel, or
bear.
Think of their good, their pleasure,
or their gain;
Think of those round thee—it will
not be vain.

Interred in September;
a C. Titus. y. % =. ". Gould ..
